{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive","id":645020,"title":"How do conspiracys survive?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-29T23:08:31-07:00","id":645020,"title":"How do conspiracys survive?","content":"Something that's confused me. Let's say a conspiracy sets themselves up in a certain location. They spot a (werewolf, vampire, creature from the black lagoon, ect). And kill it. Then they find another one and kill it as well, then another, and another. And if somehow the hunters are still alive I would assume that the local (insert hunted creature here) population would start looking into the random deaths, eventually leading them to kill the hunters, or forcing the hunters to retreat and get back up. More hunters arrive and there is all out war. The conspiracy would likely win the first time, but then it would happen again, and again. Until they all died or the conspiracy becomes a compact as most of them die. So how exactly do they function when they have a &quot;kill on sight&quot; motto and organized supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","name":"Andresmo23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T23:22:38-07:00","id":645046,"title":"","content":"they would have to find proof of the conspiracy and some sort of listing of members that almost certainly wouldnt exist,, then be actually able to kill those hunters without others finding out and going to ground or organizing a defense, and organize their own efforts which there is no real guarantee they can, and keep other supernaturals from finding out what they are doing because those might decide to work with the conspiracy to get rid of you, and ensure mortal authorities dont notice the hundreds of targeted murders going on around the city. a conspiracy that cant survive doesn't become a conspiracy in the first place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T01:05:00-07:00","id":645145,"title":"","content":"Willing suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they would have to find proof of the conspiracy and some sort of listing of members that almost certainly wouldnt exist,, </div> </div> </div>Why? I mean, such an attack looks like the work of multiple people, and all you need to investigate is suspicion. Plus the supernatural creatures generally have mind control or telepathy of some kind. You can just ask members who else is in their group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a conspiracy that cant survive doesn't become a conspiracy in the first place </div> </div> </div>It's fiction, so that's not true at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T04:09:41-07:00","id":645239,"title":"","content":"Simple. In most cases the Conspiracy would win an all out war with monsters.<br /> <br /> Endowments (except Castigation) can be given to anyone. Werewolf numbers are finite. Back in 1E five to ten Hunters with Endowments were a match for just about any supernatural except a high level Mage, Mummy or Ephemerial Being. Chances are that will be the case again with 2E Endowments; and Hunters could get five to ten fighters per monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T05:08:59-07:00","id":645292,"title":"","content":"There is always the fact that the monsters being hunted are not an internationally organized body of like-minded and disciplined people. They are a fractured bunch that do not communicate well on anything more than a regional level and even at a regional level they are often wracked by internal politics that can get extremely bloody at times. What is more, their ability to act tends to be tied since they have to keep up at least some pretense of secrecy. Not just because of humanity, but also because of their own supernatural enemies. A large amount of deaths is not going to help keeping a low profile. Besides, there is always the arrogance in that they belief that the hunter groups are a great pawns to use against other monsters. Not to mention that the sane, well-adjusted monsters are unlikely to even draw the attention of the hunters. It are the insane and depraved amongst themselves who draw such attention, and if somebody else takes care of them, good riddance. Why do you think Hunters tend to think of the others as monsters? Those are the opponents they tend to face.<br /> <br /> The conspiracies on the other hand are disciplined, organized and well trained to keep their secrets hidden. Most of their agents also know very little about the upper echelons of their organization and as such can betray very little when caught. The organization leadership likely has some backups hidden, and that is assuming they are not actually supernaturals themselves (which is certainly true for some of the conspiracies). I also doubt that they would stick to one town, trying to eradicate everything non-human. For one thing, there are not enough Hunters to do so and a well-adjusted monster stays below the radar. Hunters of a conspiracy tend to go to a place to investigate a specific case and leave when they have dealt with it. It are the lower tiered hunter groups that stick to one place, but those either end up disbanding, dead or as pawns eventually and if destroyed a new similar group rises later on with similar believes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T07:11:44-07:00","id":645376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=645239#post645239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple. In most cases the Conspiracy would win an all out war with monsters.<br /> <br /> Endowments (except Castigation) can be given to anyone. Werewolf numbers are finite. Back in 1E five to ten Hunters with Endowments were a match for just about any supernatural except a high level Mage, Mummy or Ephemerial Being. Chances are that will be the case again with 2E Endowments; and Hunters could get five to ten fighters per monster.</div> </div> </div> </div> Conspiracies number on average 1000 agents. So that's half a global organization's entire force to deal with say 50 werewolves, and if an elder calls a crusade and 300 or 400 closest lycanthropic friends come to eliminate this grave threat to the werewolves' sacred laws of secrecy, the entire conspiracy is now facing 3 or 2 to 1 odds, and is totally screwed by your own math. <br /> <br /> There's a reason the gameline is called Hunter, and not Space Marine: The Prequel.<br /> <br /> And werewolves don't have finite numbers, new ones are produced by Luna's whims, if she decided she needed another million werewolves she's going to produce another million werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T09:00:46-07:00","id":645455,"title":"","content":"Conspiracies draw from hypothetical conspiracies in real life as a general principle, so they survive in similar ways- hiding among lots of numbers, lots of dummy set-ups that can be stepped up at any moment, striking when they have the game overwhelmingly stacked, and more or less just playing the paranoid game as best they can.<br /> <br /> Something to consider is that we, as players and readers, know that the conspiracies have bases in Athens, Milan, Rome, etc., but the monsters don't, or at least, didn't know about for a long time. The Conspiracies kept up their veil of secrecy long enough to become established powers where they settled in, and decentralized enough that they can no longer just hit one place and win.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's another thing, the supernatural aren't actually coordinated all that well. Sure, the Tribes exist around the world, but the focus for werewolves at the Pack level and the expectation is that local wolves deal with local problems. The Courts in 1E and the Covenants are shared ideologies and structures, but there's little actual communication between cities-and in 2E, Courts are now less global than they were, with each city now having a choice between traditional courts and new ones. Throngs are as much grouping as you get in Promethean, and that's not going to take down a Conspiracy anytime soon. Krewes generally also exist on the Throng/Pack level as Cults, and the second common structure for them, Factions, tend towards a small region. The Guilds are global affairs, with some decent structure too, but the Arisen have to weigh in their time value versus their duties, and often times the Conspiracies aren't large enough to merit actual attention within their timeframe. It falls to the cults to figure out if it's worth that, and most cults do't actually work with other cults to coordinate that sort of thing. Demonic Agencies are focused on their local region, and those are really more informational networks most of the time. Beasts <i>might</i> have the capacity to pull together broods(Including all of the former) on the right sort of scale to do it, but they consider a fair number of conspiracies as troublesome kin and often would need to invest in building up presence. Mages are the only ones who have the human tendency to look beyond their area and collaborate on the sort of scale that can handle conspiracies now, and they have better things to do.<br /> <br /> The point is that the Conspiracies have stayed alive by staying quiet and sneaky and the right kind of populous enough throughout the ages long enough to become both powerful enough, wide enough, and connected enough to be able to square off against the more factitious monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T10:09:04-07:00","id":645544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=645376#post645376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conspiracies number on average 1000 agents. So that's half a global organization's entire force to deal with say 50 werewolves, and if an elder calls a crusade and 300 or 400 closest lycanthropic friends come to eliminate this grave threat to the werewolves' sacred laws of secrecy, the entire conspiracy is now facing 3 or 2 to 1 odds, and is totally screwed by your own math.</div> </div> </div> </div>General rule of the WoD, if it ever gives out specific population numbers, ignore them. 1000 is rediculously low, and puts TF:V as smaller than the New York Police department despite covering the better part of two continents - and since it says TF:V is the largest, it gets even more rediculous when you imagine how thin the MM must be spread across six continents.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T10:37:12-07:00","id":645557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conspiracies draw from hypothetical conspiracies in real life as a general principle, </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting point. The supernaturals of the NWoD have relatively 'realistic' social set ups (ie. highly localised and prone to falling apart, it always reminded me of the way organsied crime in the real world is described). In comparison the Hunter conspiracies draw on much less realistic material with these massive conspiracies and that can make for a very odd comparison. If this were the CWoD, no one would notice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1000 is rediculously low, and puts TF:V as smaller than the New York Police department despite covering the better part of two continents - and since it says TF:V is the largest, it gets even more rediculous when you imagine how thin the MM must be spread across six continents. </div> </div> </div>I think the bigger issue is the question of whether conspiracies actually settle down in an area or not (sometimes they do, sometimes they don't). Their size could work if they just sent groups out to do specific tasks; I mean TFV seems to have a size not that far off a real life intelligence agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T11:29:17-07:00","id":645628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=645557#post645557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very interesting point. The supernaturals of the NWoD have relatively 'realistic' social set ups (ie. highly localised and prone to falling apart, it always reminded me of the way organsied crime in the real world is described). In comparison the Hunter conspiracies draw on much less realistic material with these massive conspiracies and that can make for a very odd comparison. If this were the CWoD, no one would notice.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you think about it though. The Catholic Church has successfully run evil conspiracies in the real world. So I don't find it hard to imagine that in the WoD they'd be able to run another. The USA government, I could buy them running a stable conspiracy. The Ascending Ones are as factious as the Pentacle (if a little less violent aobut it). The Lucifgue are tiny.<br /> <br /> Of the core six only the AKD really stretches belief. But basically. Big Hunter Conspiracies are big, respectable and stable mortal institutions running black book operations. So comparing them to a goverment conspiracy instead of organised crime makes sense - and government conspiracies are often less stable and localised than organised crime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=645557#post645557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bigger issue is the question of whether conspiracies actually settle down in an area or not (sometimes they do, sometimes they don't). Their size could work if they just sent groups out to do specific tasks; I mean TFV seems to have a size not that far off a real life intelligence agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>TF:V cannonically covers the entire NATO area, MM probably covers most of the world with significant catholic presence.<br /> <br /> Also the NSA is estimated at 30,000 - 40,000 members. That's significantly larger than TF:V's 8,000. What's more TF:V covers a much much larger area than the NSA/FBI and is the only official USA monster hunters. Even VASCU are technically after mortal serial killers. The NSA splits the workload with the Alphabet Soup.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T19:23:27-07:00","id":646201,"title":"","content":"I think everyone's made some good points about most of Andresmo23's query.<br /> <br /> Just to throw in something, it's probably worth noting that not every conspiracy has a kill on sight motto. The Ascending Ones are quite diplomatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T00:54:27-07:00","id":646426,"title":"","content":"I vwouldn't compare TF:V directly with the NSA especially not in regards of numbers. They have a very specific purpose, aiming at a relatively small segment of the 'criminal world', especially if you consider that most sleeper servants of the supernatural threat are dealt with by sleeper agencies. What is more, those 1000 are probably all active members fully aware of the supernatural world. Most of those NSA operatives are probably office workers involved in data analysis and support roles, something they do for TF:V as well. You do not need to know vampires exist to realize find specific patterns of deaths, you only need to know to send the alert to a specific mail address when you do find it.<br /> <br /> As for kill on sight, I doubt any hunter conspiracies is going to be that blatant about it. It gets you killed real quick and is unlikely to solve the problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:01:51-07:00","id":647118,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned: Narrative Causality combined with several of them being controlled by non-Hunters -- TFV by Vampires, Lucifuge by (maybe) an Angel of the God-Machine, Cheiron Group by. . .the astral projection of aliens, or whatever. And I'd be more than willing to bet that even if others aren't outright controlled by major splats, there are Vampires, Seers, etc. out there who would think &quot;I bet misdirecting Hunters could come in handy&quot; rather than &quot;murdertime&quot;.<br /> <br /> As far as the book's concerned: because Hunters don't go up against Major Templates. As much as nWoD is cross-over compatible (if not friendly), the Hunter goes out of it's way several times across several books to say: don't use Mage, use all this stuff from Witch Finders. Make your Vampires, Werewolves, etc. with Dread Powers. Is it also because they're being nice and not saying &quot;if you want to run Hunter, better buy all the other books too!&quot;? Yes. But it's also rather pointed about using Dread Powers instead of full-on Templates, because full-on Templates are TERRIFYING to mortals/Hunters. Anything Hunters can do, Major Templates can do better. Except, sometimes, stand in sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T18:01:38-07:00","id":647463,"title":"","content":"A conspiracy has an interest in keeping their Vigil a secret from the world. At most, they might expose an individual, not supernatural organizations. Rarely, would a conspiracy actually know how numerous a given group of supernaturals might be, so they are cautious. Mortals, if they knew the truth about supernaturals, could wage a war and the mortals would win against even a combined effort of all supernaturals. The cost in death to eliminate one group would be difficult to imagine. So even if KOS is the motto, it still falls short of all out war. It isn't worth it for all parties involved. A cell doesn't worry about the big picture. A compact is still too small to pull off anything so big. A conspiracy has leaders that know they will never &quot;win&quot; the war so they focus on battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T05:14:02-07:00","id":647872,"title":"","content":"3 words: Vampiric Sugar-daddies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T05:17:07-07:00","id":647876,"title":"","content":"It's also worth mentioning that, since a group of Hunters is a Cell, there's an implied amount of operational security going on. Can't mind-rape information about an organization from a Hunter's skull if they don't know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:49:31-07:00","id":649532,"title":"","content":"It is in the nature of a conspiracy to hide themselves from view. Part of the reason they don't use what power they have to blow the lid off the supernatural and get the whole planet in on the Vigil is because doing so would also expose them to the monsters that rule the universe.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that part of the reason they survive is because they have been subtly compromised to one degree or another. Just enough that one supernatural patron or another finds them useful to have around and helps shield them from other outside meddling. This is emphatically 'not' the same thing as control though. These are organizations that melt into the paperwork and live in forgotten institutional folkways. Their bureaucratic autonomy is not easily suborned and regulatory capture remains an insidious factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:20:19-07:00","id":659392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=647118#post647118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucifuge by (maybe) an Angel of the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is this written in one of the books? Because I would really like to know if Lady Lucifuge is an Angel, God Machine, Half-Angel, Half-Demon .etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T21:34:05-07:00","id":660317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=659392#post659392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is this written in one of the books? Because I would really like to know if Lady Lucifuge is an Angel, God Machine, Half-Angel, Half-Demon .etc</div> </div> </div> </div> It goes over it on page 131 and 132 of Hunter: Mortal Remains. Far from concrete that she's. . .well, anything at all, but it's presented that one of the three groups within the Lucifuge think the Lady could be an agent of the God Machine, maybe even an Angel. And that maybe the Unchained they're hunting (presented as Greater Demons in that book) are merely flaws in the Great Machine, and the Lucifuge is acting as white blood cells for said Machine.<br /> <br /> It's interesting and I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:02:23-07:00","id":665901,"title":"","content":"A couple of answers:<br /> <br /> 1. Sometimes they don't. Sometimes the enemy wins and dismantles the organization. However...<br /> <br /> 2. This is harder than it might seem just by looking at pure supernatural advantage. Human groups have some organizational advantages, and most importantly, aren't as endangered by blowing the masquerade; overt counterattacks by, say, vampires, at a bunch of government employees engaged in classified work would attract a lot of attention. It does the Invictus no good to shut down Task Force Valkyrie if World War Vampire is the result. The supernatural communities are mostly balkanized, they have huge incentives to stay under anyone's radar, and they've already got investments in keeping the local masquerade afloat. As powerful as a given city's prince is, he might not have any ability to counterattack against Valkyrie in Washington DC. So he can maybe take out the cell bothering his city, but another might well show up later. Coordinating the destruction of a major hunter conspiracy would take a major supernatural conspiracy, and those groups can't always get that kind of thing organized. <br /> <br /> 3. Look at it from the supernatural perspective. Say City X has a really good cell of hunters apparently backed by the government (for example). They've taken heavy casualties and call for backup. Does a neighboring group (coterie, cabal, etc) risk themselves and risk conflict with an evidently dangerous group of mortals? Some of the supernaturals will be risking their immortality, or their obsessed investigations into a local mystery, to stick their neck out like that. Even the groups dedicated to defensive actions (the Invictus, etc) have limited resources and information. So the full on counter-attack is just as likely as, say, a political accommodation or tacit coordination or avoidance or alliance. And all the supernaturals have problems of their own. &quot;I've got three good killers I can use to strike back at these mortals,&quot; says the Invictus shot-caller in Baltimore, &quot;But if I lose any of them the Carthians will strike while we're weak...I can use the Sheriff as well, but I've got him tracking down reports of Strix...&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. It's not all that easy to take down a hunter group using cell structure, compartmentalization, security precautions. They'll know their enemy's main weaknesses and capabilities, some of them have supernatural tricks up their sleeves as well, conspiracies are well distributed enough to rebuild themselves even after heavy losses, etc. <br /> <br /> 5. But, basically, there's no guarantee a given conspiracy survives. They're not immune. Some die out, others emerge, the Vigil continues. They win some battles, they lose others. Supernatural groups are at least as vulnerable; there's nothing guaranteeing the Invictus is still around in a hundred years, or the Pentacle survives the Great Seer Attack of 2035, or any werewolves live long enough to find a cure for the weaponized viral idigam engineered by Cheiron and put into popular energy drinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:43:05-07:00","id":668966,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of victim-blaming among monsters. If a vampire gets taken out by hunters, it's their fault for being shitty. The Masquerade is far from zero-defect, it's about containment. And so forth. It takes a dramatic and easily tracked campaign for supernaturals to feel collectively threatened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T08:30:08-07:00","id":670990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=647463#post647463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals, if they knew the truth about supernaturals, could wage a war and the mortals would win against even a combined effort of all supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are talking about NWoD as a unified cosmology with full Greater Template supernaturals, this is just directly false. The best humanity could hope for would be a return to the status quo where the fight isn't worth continuing, so the supernaturals go back to ground.<br /> <br /> Humanity would have no chance against the stronger splats, especially not in a genocidal no-holds-barred war. The only things that keep the splats contained are fear of each other and infighting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:52:25-07:00","id":671381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we are talking about NWoD as a unified cosmology with full Greater Template supernaturals, this is just directly false. The best humanity could hope for would be a return to the status quo where the fight isn't worth continuing, so the supernaturals go back to ground.<br /> <br /> Humanity would have no chance against the stronger splats, especially not in a genocidal no-holds-barred war. The only things that keep the splats contained are fear of each other and infighting. </div> </div> </div>That may be so, but it's actually irrelevant to Diggs' point. The difference between 'we can't beat the supernatual' and 'it'd be so costly as to be pointless' is basically irrelevant. Especially considering we're discussing what conspiracies themselves believe (and we don't have great reason to believe that many of them are particularly clued-in).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T20:38:16-07:00","id":672830,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think it comes down to a number of different factors such as:<br /> <br /> 1. Conspiracies tend to have a fair amount of resources with which they can hide some of their activities. Yeah that werewolf may have been hunted down and killed but does anyone really know if they can't find the body/murder scene?<br /> <br /> 2. Many supernaturals have this idea that they are at the top or near top of the food chain and don't consider the idea of a group of humans waging a coordinated war against them very plausible. <br /> <br /> 3. Sure some supernaturals get killed but what proof do their peers have that this was done by a large scale group of humans with wide ranging power across the globe? More than likely they think the killers are a local group of pissed off or extremely deviant humans (the latter being the most likely conclusion when the Abbey rolls into town for a night of &quot;fun&quot;) thus creating a weird kind of smokescreen for the larger, usually more cautious groups.<br /> <br /> 4. Many conspiracies seem to have this here today, gone tomorrow MO. They're basically Mulder and Scully coming in, dealing with a particularly obvious problem, and then leaving right afterwards so while they do rack up a body count it's across large areas and given that most supernatural groups don't necessarily communicate across long distances very often it's not likely they'd put two and two together.<br /> <br /> 5. Some conspiracies are likely to operate using a public front. Very few werewolves, vampires, etc would suspect that the Cheiron Group that just set up the factory downtown actually has a secret level in the building for processing their most interesting &quot;acquisitions&quot; especially if they disappear without a trace.<br /> <br /> 6. Some conspiracies might be suspected to exist but no evidence can be found or they're obfuscated by myths and misdirection. TFV pretty much can hide behind the men in black nonsense to some extent despite the fact that some supernaturals suspect that the government probably has some kind of monster buster unit because it cleaves a little too close to what the nutcases keep saying. Many might hear whispers that the Inquisition is alive and well but most would dismiss it as an unproven conspiracy theory. Many would outright dismiss the origin and motives of the Lucifuge even if someone respected brought up the idea just because it sounds so crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T23:57:35-07:00","id":672958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Many supernaturals have this idea that they are at the top or near top of the food chain and don't consider the idea of a group of humans waging a coordinated war against them very plausible. </div> </div> </div>Why would they assume that? The various supernatural groups themselves use conspiracies. If you believe that, you'd assume that some other supernatural group is attacking you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T00:45:04-07:00","id":672974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=672958#post672958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they assume that? The various supernatural groups themselves use conspiracies. If you believe that, you'd assume that some other supernatural group is attacking you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the assumption in this context is that the hunter conspiracies are not 'supernatural'. Mind you, most supernaturals (in 1e Vampire, Werewolf, Mage and Changeling anyway) actually do not really operate on a global conspiracy level in regards to humanity. They rarely manipulate humans beyond the county or at most country level. Since they are not globally organized, why would they assume that group of hunters is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:10:49-07:00","id":673426,"title":"","content":"To add to the thread, the murders committed by the various conspiracies will mostly go unnoticed, as there are relatively few supernaturals who exist among normal society in any legitimate way. Fake licenses and IDs I would imagine are rampant, if carried at all, and the murders covered up by whole societies of supernaturals that want to protect the masquerade/veil/what-have-you.<br /> <br /> As the supernatural population gets culled of it's most obvious members the crime and murder rates are actually likely to decrease in the public eye as there are fewer actual civilians with paper-trails and bodies being eaten in the night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=672974#post672974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the assumption in this context is that the hunter conspiracies are not 'supernatural'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that TFV at least is directly run/funded by vampires.<br /> <br /> Likewise, when Michael says that the other supernaturals use conspiracies, there is more than one way to do that. It wouldn't surprise me if unethical Mages make regular deals / infiltrate the Cheiron Group, or Vampires that use Net0 to expose rivals to masquerade violations. The conspiracies don't need to be controlled by supernaturals globally to be indispensable to the schemes of enough supernaturals as to warrant protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:24:34-07:00","id":673432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the assumption in this context is that the hunter conspiracies are not 'supernatural'. </div> </div> </div>To clarify my point which was not very well made. If a reasonably professional group of hunters attacks you; a sensible person is going to want to investigate that a bit. Who are they? Where were they trained? Most importantly, who is out to get me? Even if the supernatural being in question assumes it can't possibly be mortals; they're still going to investigate, because they'll assume it's another supernatural creature. My point is, the asummption doesn't actually protect the conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since they are not globally organized, why would they assume that group of hunters is? </div> </div> </div>This made me think of another possible explanation for conspiracy survival: distance. Even if you dominate a member of the Lucifuge into giving you the address and phone number of the Lucifuge herself, you generally still have to go to Milan; and it's a largely unknown quantity there. It seems pretty plausible to me that a lot of supernatural beings could have a rough idea of who runs the MM or the Lucifuge (even if it's as vague as 'a group in Milan'), but see leaving their own turf as not worth the risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T16:07:18-07:00","id":673521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=673432#post673432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To clarify my point which was not very well made. If a reasonably professional group of hunters attacks you; a sensible person is going to want to investigate that a bit. Who are they? Where were they trained? Most importantly, who is out to get me? Even if the supernatural being in question assumes it can't possibly be mortals; they're still going to investigate, because they'll assume it's another supernatural creature. My point is, the asummption doesn't actually protect the conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This made me think of another possible explanation for conspiracy survival: distance. Even if you dominate a member of the Lucifuge into giving you the address and phone number of the Lucifuge herself, you generally still have to go to Milan; and it's a largely unknown quantity there. It seems pretty plausible to me that a lot of supernatural beings could have a rough idea of who runs the MM or the Lucifuge (even if it's as vague as 'a group in Milan'), but see leaving their own turf as not worth the risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify my point which was I admit rushed and a bit lacking in detail many supernaturals cultural beliefs and accepted truths can end up working in the conspiracy's favor. Vampires and mages have been known to get it into their heads that they are far superior to humans. Werewolves will deal with humans when necessary but often try to keep to the periphery. Changelings tend to fear their old masters more than they do humans and put their focus elsewhere. Promotheans are still trying to figure out what it means to be human and may not have discovered the idea of a herd mentality yet. Many of these groups also live with the general idea that they live in the shadows, going under the radar, and that the most massive breaches are generally dealt with because if they don't humanity will rise like a tide to smother them all. Add to that the more &quot;mundane&quot; and plausible explanations the supernatural can come to and the idea they hit upon there being a giant human conspiracy gunning for all supernaturals is far less likely to occur.<br /> <br /> To look at your example let's say a vampire is attack by a group of well armed and knowledgeable humans. They could be ghouls, blood dolls, smucks on the street hired by a rival, a small group of people victimized by vampires and out for revenge, etc. All of these are more plausible than them being part of a crack global strike force out for the vampire and all of its ilk. Similarly for werewolves they could just be people who are spirit possessed and for changelings they could be the fair folk in disguise. Point being your immediate focus is on what you are familiar with rather than diverging into the more outlandish. Keep in mind that conspiracies are generally not amateurs and don't make the usual mistakes as Anachronistic pointed out and often set up ways of misdirecting prey to one of the more &quot;obvious&quot; conclusions rather than to there doorstep (or set things up so if the supernatural does make it to their doorstep it has no hope of escape).<br /> <br /> Finally again as Anachronistic pointed out there are probably some supernaturals that have found out about a given conspiracy and haven't outed them yet. This usually takes two forms and the supernatural either A: Tries to subtly manipulate the organization so as to avoid exposure and to benefit itself in some way such as sending them after rivals or B: Realizes that if news of a large scale, well equipped, coordinated, but not omniscient human effort at the extermination of them and their ilk is known it will cause panic that would only serve to make things worse including possibly ripping the veil from all the sheeples' eyes. In the latter case they may try to subtly subvert the organization trying to weaken it without getting caught while doing their best to spread disinformation about the group's existence to avoid the panic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T12:53:57-07:00","id":674490,"title":"","content":"I think there's a clever idea there, I just don't think any of the conspiracies really do that. I think that's one of the oversights of Hunter that it doesn't really go into the hunter's masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They could be ghouls, blood dolls, smucks on the street hired by a rival, a small group of people victimized by vampires and out for revenge, etc. All of these are more plausible than them being part of a crack global strike force out for the vampire and all of its ilk. </div> </div> </div>That's true, I agree. But that vampire is still going to investigate the people who attacked them if they think it's one of those options you present. Someone is attacking them, and a reasonable response is to look for who that is. and unless the cell have done work to cover their tracks, it's going to lead back to the Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Another possibility this raises is that the conspiracies tend to go in so hard on individual areas that the supernatural beings just don't have the opporunity to seek revenge. That's not really presented in the book but I'm struggling to see any other way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T14:55:59-07:00","id":674600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=674490#post674490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility this raises is that the conspiracies tend to go in so hard on individual areas that the supernatural beings just don't have the opporunity to seek revenge. That's not really presented in the book but I'm struggling to see any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, again, even if they do get noticed the big players will try to use them and the small fries won't have the capability to take them on. The only time I can see it being a real problem for the survival of a conspiracy is if they happened to get (un)lucky enough to go after a big player in a meaningful way - at which point they either succeed and scare everyone else to ground, having proven they aren't to be messed with, or they fail and have the dedicated enmity of a powerful supernatural with the resources to make it a problem.<br /> <br /> I see that latter option as unlikely though, the dangerous fish in NWoD are so good at covering their tracks from mortals that it's hardly even funny. They are, as they say, behind seven proxies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:50:33-07:00","id":674656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, again, even if they do get noticed the big players will try to use them and the small fries won't have the capability to take them on. </div> </div> </div>I'd treat that as effectively the same outcome. You've either died or become the thing you fought against. I'm coming at this from the perspective that these strategies shouldn't generally involve saying that that has already happened (though there are a good number where that's exactly what happened).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:51:34-07:00","id":674657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=674490#post674490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a clever idea there, I just don't think any of the conspiracies really do that. I think that's one of the oversights of Hunter that it doesn't really go into the hunter's masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's true, I agree. But that vampire is still going to investigate the people who attacked them if they think it's one of those options you present. Someone is attacking them, and a reasonable response is to look for who that is. and unless the cell have done work to cover their tracks, it's going to lead back to the Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Another possibility this raises is that the conspiracies tend to go in so hard on individual areas that the supernatural beings just don't have the opporunity to seek revenge. That's not really presented in the book but I'm struggling to see any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but remember what I said: The conspiracies aren't amateurs. They know how to deal with supernaturals that manage to survive and are likely using more than one of the options I presented and you can bet that one of them is covering their tracks with misleading evidence. This also brings up another possibility: The conspiracy may have let the vampire go. Usually it's not the sharpest knives in the drawer that manage to get noticed. Maybe the conspiracy actually is being run by one of the bigwigs and the dumbass being targeted is being taught a lesson. Perhaps it's even more sinister than that. Perhaps the conspiracy wants to mislead the dumbass into kicking off a vampiric turf war that thins their numbers while the conspiracy sits back in the shadows waiting to pick off the weakened survivors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T00:44:23-07:00","id":675011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=674490#post674490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, I agree. But that vampire is still going to investigate the people who attacked them if they think it's one of those options you present. Someone is attacking them, and a reasonable response is to look for who that is. and unless the cell have done work to cover their tracks, it's going to lead back to the Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Another possibility this raises is that the conspiracies tend to go in so hard on individual areas that the supernatural beings just don't have the opporunity to seek revenge. That's not really presented in the book but I'm struggling to see any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes the vampires become aware of the hunters before they leave again. In my mind, most Tier 3 hunter groups deal with specific cases. A good hunting group remains hidden until they strike, and they disappear as quickly as possible afterwards, in case of a tier 3 group likely another city if not another country. Vampires, and most other supernaturals, are simply not organized enough on a global scale to do much investigation on that scale. One thing is for sure, a tier 3 group that does not work to cover their tracks is going to be cut loose by their own organization (likely in a violent way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T07:42:55-07:00","id":675227,"title":"","content":"Has anyone brought up the possibility that supernaturals are of the opinion that Hunter conspiracies are a secondary objective compared to other, more powerful adversaries. <br /> <br /> Infighting between supernaturals is fairly common for religious and political reasons especially within the same splat.<br /> <br /> And consider how many different sample antagonist creatures come packed in every book.<br /> <br /> There's honestly not enough time to wipe out hunters with everything else trying to kill the monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:30:46-07:00","id":675703,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Something that bears considering is a given Conspiracy's operational profile in a specific locality. Even TFV isn't going to kick in the door with the goal of eradicating every bloodsucker, shapeshifter, and sorceror within city limits. They're going to go after particular targets that either have something the Conspiracy wants or who's removal would work towards solving a bigger problem. They're also not above using proxies of their own. The books suggest that Conspiracies will recruit and supply lower tier hunter cells to do their dirty work while distancing themselves from exposure. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Then there's the matter of convincing your local Primogen/Alphas/Cabal of what's really happening. Even if you know the man behind all the seemingly unrelated disappearances over the last decade is a mysterious pharma rep with bees coming out of his arm and a fleet of black vans, you're going to have a difficult time rallying enough credulous support to go after him. Presuming you've done so the best you can hope for is to make your city hard for them to operate in, maybe even drive them out. The more you learn about them though the more questions there are and the crazier the story starts to sound. You'd need the resources and resolve of an entire Convenant to go after a Conspiracy in all out war. Another difficult sell.<br /> <br /> Even then, you might lay havoc on the lower and mid level cells of the Conspiracy, but their leaders are going to make a habit of slipping through your fingers and the core ethos of the Conspiracy is just going to morph into a new form. Task Force Valkyrie is officially disavowed and dissolved by the U.S. government, but somewhere in a black budget line item there's a project called MKTWILIGHT that quietly sets up shop. Cheiron Group is dismantled as a corporate entity and its assets auctioned off, then a brilliant but troubled med student is inspired to perform dangerous experiments by a medieval tome bearing Cheiron's likeness.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T00:22:55-07:00","id":678607,"title":"","content":"Conspiracies continue to exist via having a patron, central ideals and traditions, and a common enemy.<br /> <br /> Cheiron - &gt; exploiting the supernatural for fun and profit (cut out the font company ideal, it's refreshing just to have an enemy has straightforward reasons why their evil/morally grey)<br /> <br /> TF:V and friends - &gt; protecting and projecting US influence and stability onto the supernatural.<br /> <br /> MM - &gt; protecting catholic communities around the world with patronage from the Vatican.<br /> <br /> And so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> A tier 3, it's less about the enemy you are fighting and very much the reason of why you are fighting that dictates the reason for existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T11:13:42-07:00","id":679187,"title":"","content":"And lets not forget the colossal leap it takes to associate a singular threat with a world-spanning conspiracy. Especially considering most World of Darkness supernatural factions are localized and have little in the vein of global connections.<br /> <br /> Surely your characters have come up against a threat. A monster, a human, another supernatural. Did you think they were one of many, and that similar attacks were going on around the entire world? And, most importantly, that you should do something about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T12:14:54-07:00","id":679250,"title":"","content":"More operationally, in case this hasn't been mentioned yet, a conspiracy bureaucracy can work to an advantage as well. As gargantuan as they seem, it's established that most conspiracies keep their people in the dark as far as giving them a wider scope is concerned. Oh how terrible, MRU-216 was compromised. Did they know anything important? No? Well write up a quick cover story and establish a replacement.<br /> <br /> Another factor is money. As we all agree, TFV being in vampiric pockets was lame. But TFV operating within the budgets of the FBI, DoD, et al, that's millions of dollars to creativly appropriate. Add in organizations like the Postal Service and Transportation, and you have the national network to move through as a cover. And that's just TFV, imagine the connections of the Catholic Church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:03:55-07:00","id":679281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=679250#post679250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More operationally, in case this hasn't been mentioned yet, a conspiracy bureaucracy can work to an advantage as well. As gargantuan as they seem, it's established that most conspiracies keep their people in the dark as far as giving them a wider scope is concerned. Oh how terrible, MRU-216 was compromised. Did they know anything important? No? Well write up a quick cover story and establish a replacement.<br /> <br /> Another factor is money. As we all agree, TFV being in vampiric pockets was lame. But TFV operating within the budgets of the FBI, DoD, et al, that's millions of dollars to creativly appropriate. Add in organizations like the Postal Service and Transportation, and you have the national network to move through as a cover. And that's just TFV, imagine the connections of the Catholic Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always viewed the Kindred connection to be irksome (without Abe being involved to justify it) and either be replaced via la God Machine (all that fancy tech has to come from somewhere), or simply drop that angle all together as TFV guarding the machines that print the world's reserve currency being reason enough to justify the expenses that they have.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:17:28-07:00","id":679294,"title":"","content":"I personally don't like the God-Machine angle, and a loose rule of thumb for most people I've talked about the subject with is that the US government has tech a good 10-15 years beyond what they let people know about.<br /> <br /> The other factor in terms of operations is who you place where. Conspiracies have a clear division of labor, and even with moments Right Hand / Left Hand, the cover-up people are trained to handle when the leg-breakers screw up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T13:45:17-07:00","id":679310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=679281#post679281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always viewed the Kindred connection to be irksome (without Abe being involved to justify it)</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm a fan of Vampire Abe, I always had Vampire Abe consider himself to be an American and not a Vampire and have no personal contacts or ties to Vampire society.<br /> <br /> BTW, speaking of TFV and vampires, Flyboy you seen my Counter Cultural USA yet? Link in my sig.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T15:32:02-07:00","id":679389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/645020-how-do-conspiracys-survive?p=679250#post679250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another factor is money. As we all agree, TFV being in vampiric pockets was lame. But TFV operating within the budgets of the FBI, DoD, et al, that's millions of dollars to creativly appropriate. Add in organizations like the Postal Service and Transportation, and you have the national network to move through as a cover. And that's just TFV, imagine the connections of the Catholic Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually liked Task Force Valkyrie's vampire connection.<br /> <br /> But in regards to the rest, it would be easy to frame up a cell as some ex-military people with a personal grudge against whomever they were hunting. Groups like the Malleus Maleficarum can probably lose paper trails easily, if they even have them to begin with. The Ascending Ones is a criminal organization who've been keeping secrets for thousands for years. Aegis Kai Doru probably has a lot of paper trails, considering how sending things work, but also have the magic to do something about it. Cheiron is probably the most publicly accessible, but you have the Pentex problem, where those strangers you saw with a vampire before he disappeared worked for LabCorp, which has five or six subsidiaries between it and Pentex, and were sent to another division across the country. I think TFV and Cheiron, though, which seem the most 'organized' of the conspiracies, are also called out to have overwatch when out on the hunt, with someone staying back from the cell who can make calls to command from safety if things go haywire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}